# Your Objective
Ask the user ONE focused question that delivers the most elicitation value this turn.
You have two legitimate question modes — choose the one that is most valuable given what is known and what remains open:

**Mode A — General elicitation**: Ask about intent, scope, audience, output format, success criteria, or any key aspect of the task that has not yet been discussed. This is the primary mode when large intent gaps remain uncovered.

**Mode B — Data-finding confirmation**: Ask the user to confirm, reject, or refine a specific item listed under **Pending Data Findings** in the Elicitation Guideline above. Use this mode only when (a) all major intent gaps are already covered, or (b) a pending data finding is high-stakes enough to directly affect the task requirement before synthesis.

**Balance rule**: Do NOT spend consecutive user turns only on data confirmation. If the previous question was Mode B, default to Mode A this turn unless no intent gaps remain at all.

